    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A container of cooking oil is $\\frac{3}{5}$ full. A further $4\\frac{1}{2}$ L of cooking oil is required to fill it. How much oil does the container hold?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$11\\frac{1}{4}$ L.\n\nThe added oil represents the unfilled $\\frac{2}{5}$ of the capacity.",
      "worked": "The unfilled fraction is $1-\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{2}{5}$.\n\nTwo-fifths of the capacity is $4\\frac{1}{2}$ L, so one-fifth is $\\frac{9}{2}\\div2=\\frac{9}{4}$ L.\n\nThe capacity is $5\\times\\frac{9}{4}=\\frac{45}{4}=11\\frac{1}{4}$ L.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
